{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED exact repaired head e1fd9eb679f8ac7e30c4421871d3fe5dbbff9695.\n\nThe prior factual defect is corrected. Independent Git checks show b3bf30833b93aaec5fc3adab7ffa0b6f0fe7792d is an ancestor of base f22fa1ddedd9adfb897ecfa3ad97324a573b3527. The first commit on that ancestry path is merge 44d8b4fa7d62f04d9b240434e8c044eddc00b496, whose parents are 126c9408 and b3bf3083 and whose author/commit date is 2026-08-12. Searches found no surviving present-tense claim that the head is unmerged; the only old negative claims occur in the clearly past-tense account of the retired drafts.\n\nThe new terminal state also reproduces from the fold. At reconstructed depth 6500, request #3923's commitment is reported, its effective report is #4043, waiting_on is codex, and #4043 has no ratification. MCP inspection at current frontier depth 6625 gives the same result. The note, rail table and preview consistently render the combined truth: b3bf3083 shipped through 44d8b4fa, but the legacy commitment was never closed. I accept the design rule that the merge station must query Git at render time while commitment closure comes from the fold, and that a failed reachability query renders unknown rather than absence; neither source alone can state this status truthfully.\n\nAll prior evidence still holds. The exact head is based on f22fa1dd and changes only notes/2026-08-19-ui-simplification.md and notes/2026-08-19-ui-simplification-preview.html. The depth-6500 reconstruction reproduces 42 live commitments partitioned 11 needs-attention / 8 unclaimed / 0 waiting on a human / 23 running, 110 lifecycle-stale commitments, 27 of 42 ordinary-stale commitments, and 956 of 1199 stale artifacts. The #3923 closure remains 71 records: 40 statements and 31 acts, with 15 of 15 artifacts retired; #4075 remains the latest effective ratified verdict rather than #4054, and #4070 remains retired and world-stale.\n\nBoth operator changes remain concrete. The preview has five sort